# [CHANGE: claude-code | 2026-08-04] Colon-free stable alias for the AMD iGPU DRM node.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS (BUG-094):
# Hyprland's aquamarine backend reads AQ_DRM_DEVICES as a COLON-SEPARATED list. The obvious
# "stable" way to name a GPU — /dev/dri/by-path/pci-0000:65:00.0-card — contains colons, so
# aquamarine split it into three garbage paths, found no GPU, and aborted the whole session:
#
#     drm: Failed to canonicalize path /dev/dri/by-path/pci-0000
#     drm: Failed to canonicalize path 65
#     drm: Explicit device 00.0-card not found
#     drm: Found no gpus to use, cannot continue
#
# /dev/dri/cardN has no colons but its number is enumeration order and is NOT stable across
# boots — on this machine the NVIDIA dGPU enumerates FIRST as card1. So neither stock name is
# both stable and colon-free. This rule creates one that is.
#
# Matched on ID_PATH (the PCI address, fixed by the hardware), NOT on card number.
SUBSYSTEM=="drm", KERNEL=="card*", ENV{ID_PATH}=="pci-0000:65:00.0", SYMLINK+="dri/luminos-igpu"
